# E-Commerce track (D-172) — environment contract.
#
# Values NEVER live in this repository (D-045/D-124). Copy this file to
# `.env.local` (gitignored) and fill it in locally, or export the variables in
# the shell that runs `npm run db:migrate`.
#
# Only `drizzle-kit migrate` / `push` / `studio` need this variable;
# `npm run typecheck`, `npm run db:generate` and `npm run db:check` are offline.
#
# Local development target: the canonical PostgreSQL container from the local
# stack (D-053/D-055) — the same instance `local/scripts/apply_schema.py`
# targets. Ports/hosts are environment-specific; the value below is a
# placeholder, not a working credential.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://<user>:<password>@<host>:<port>/<database>

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local / disposable harness (D-172 Phase 2 hardening) — `docker-compose.db.yml`.
#
# `npm run db:up` starts a throwaway PostgreSQL 16 container published on
# 127.0.0.1:55432 ONLY, with the credentials below. They are the container's own
# literals from the compose file: not a secret, not reusable, and they unlock
# nothing outside the loopback harness (D-045/D-124 govern REAL credentials;
# none exist here and none is requested).
#
# `npm run smoke:db` runs the live suite ONLY when this variable is set — when it
# is absent the suite skips with a named reason rather than guessing a target.
# `npm run db:reset` refuses any target that is not loopback:55432.
#
# COMMERCE_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://commerce_smoke:commerce_smoke_local_only@127.0.0.1:55432/commerce_smoke

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Async payment callback (D-172 Phase 4 transition / §6.1) — NOT CONFIGURED.
#
# `POST /api/webhooks/payment` verifies an HMAC-SHA256 signature over the raw
# request body before it reads anything else. The shared secret below is the key
# that signature is computed with, and while this variable is unset the endpoint
# refuses every callback with 503 and processes nothing — no unverified mode
# exists, not even locally (D-171 §2.2: an absent configuration is a refusal,
# never a pass).
#
# The payment provider is now SELECTED — ZarinPal, primary (decision 10,
# owner ruling 2026-10-23) — but the inbound signing scheme above is still the
# track's OWN and provider-neutral: it gates whatever body reaches the endpoint
# and is not ZarinPal's proprietary callback format. Adapt that translation
# deliberately; never loosen this gate to make a provider fit.
#
# The value is a real credential once it is set. It belongs in `.env.local`
# (gitignored) or the deployment's secret store — never in this repository
# (D-045/D-124), and never in a test fixture.
# COMMERCE_PAYMENT_WEBHOOK_SECRET=replace-with-a-long-random-value

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Payment mode selector (D-172 §6.1) — `src/server/payments/gateway-runtime.ts`.
#
# Unset (the default) or any unrecognised value wires the ZarinPal adapter,
# which refuses while the two ZarinPal variables below are unset. A typo can
# therefore never enable the demo adapter.
#
# `mock` (case-insensitive) wires the offline mock with an AUTHORIZED outcome so
# a checkout can be exercised without any external call. Authorization alone
# leaves the order PENDING; the answer carries a
# `/api/payments/mock/callback?reference=MOCK-<orderId>` redirect, and that
# route — inert (404) unless this same variable is `mock` — runs the SAME
# `applyPaymentCallback` transition the real returns use, moving the order to
# PAID with a `MOCK-` reference and the normal audit row. Two steps, one write
# path, no faked status. Demo only — never a deployment setting: a production
# build (`NODE_ENV=production`, which `next build`/`next start` set) refuses the
# demo adapter AND this callback route with 404, whatever this variable says.
# PAYMENT_MODE=mock

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ZarinPal adapter (D-172 §6.1) — `src/server/payments/zarinpal.ts`. NOT CONFIGURED.
#
# Names only: no value here is a working credential, and none exists yet (D-045).
# While `ZARINPAL_MERCHANT_ID` or `ZARINPAL_CALLBACK_URL` is unset the adapter
# refuses to start a payment and reports the order as still unpaid — there is no
# placeholder merchant id, because a fake one would turn a configuration gap into
# a provider error an operator has to decode.
#
# `ZARINPAL_SANDBOX` defaults to `true`; set it to exactly `false` to reach the
# production host. Money is converted Toman -> Rial (x10) in one place (`tomanToRial`).
#
# `ZARINPAL_CALLBACK_URL` is the BROWSER-RETURN url, absolute, and must point at
# `GET /api/payments/zarinpal/callback` — NOT at the signed webhook. ZarinPal
# appends `?Authority=...&Status=OK|NOK` and redirects the customer's browser
# with a plain GET, which carries no HMAC and can never reach
# `POST /api/webhooks/payment`. The route behind this URL verifies the payment
# with the provider and then drives the same `PAID` transition the webhook does.
#
# This checkout path is wired (`getPaymentGateway`): with either variable unset
# every payment is refused as `UNAVAILABLE`, the order stays `PENDING`, and the
# customer is told the gateway is not connected. `PAYMENT_MODE=mock` above
# replaces it for offline demos only; the two cannot be combined.
# ZARINPAL_MERCHANT_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000-placeholder
# ZARINPAL_CALLBACK_URL=https://<your-host>/api/payments/zarinpal/callback
# ZARINPAL_SANDBOX=true

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Order-notification outbox (D-172 §6.2) — `src/server/notifications/*`. NOT SENT.
#
# The queue itself needs NO configuration: the outbox is a PostgreSQL table
# (`commerce.notification_outbox`) written in the same transaction that marks an
# order PAID, and the dispatcher drains it through `MockSmsChannel` by default —
# it records the message and sends NOTHING. That is the D-045 state: no SMS
# credential exists and none is requested.
#
# `SMS_LIVE_ENABLED` is the only switch that admits the Kavenegar adapter, and
# the value must be exactly `true` (case-insensitive). Requesting live SMS
# without the key and the sender line is a REFUSAL
# (`SMS_LIVE_MODE_MISSING_CREDENTIAL`) that claims no queue rows — never a
# silent fall back to the mock, because an operator who asked for live delivery
# must see that it did not happen.
#
# `NOTIFICATIONS_DISPATCH_TOKEN` authenticates the operator trigger
# `POST /api/internal/notifications/dispatch` as `Authorization: Bearer <token>`.
# While it is unset the endpoint answers `503 DISPATCH_NOT_CONFIGURED` and
# processes nothing — an absent configuration is a refusal, never an open door.
# There is no scheduler: a cron job or an operator call is what drains the queue,
# and NOT calling it is safe (the rows simply wait).
# SMS_LIVE_ENABLED=false
# KAVENEGAR_API_KEY=<owner-supplied-key>
# KAVENEGAR_SENDER=<owner-supplied-line>
# NOTIFICATIONS_DISPATCH_TOKEN=<long-random-operator-token>

